WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.779
With product opportunity explorer, you can analyze market trends and individual product

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:11.020
performance in the Amazon store.

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:14.109
If you're beginning your product research journey, you

00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:18.780
might want to take a look at broader category and subcategory trends to start.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:19.519
This approach

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:24.320
can help you discover popular niches without a specific product idea in mind.

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:25.625
For example,

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:31.067
if you're in the office supply space and looking for your next product idea, you could select

00:00:31.067 --> 00:00:36.400
the office products category to see a list of top performing niches within that space.

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:42.457
If you already have a specific product idea, you can take a more focused approach by searching

00:00:42.457 --> 00:00:44.860
for a related product, feature, or category.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.624
For example, let's say you sell home and

00:00:47.624 --> 00:00:51.080
kitchen products and want to enter the spice rack space.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.872
Searching for spice rack will show

00:00:53.872 --> 00:01:00.025
you specific features that customers may be looking for, like magnetic spice rack, wooden

00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:02.960
spice rack, or expandable spice rack.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.498
Sort your results by clicking the arrows next

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:11.216
to each column header to see the highest or lowest values for any metric, giving you

00:01:11.216 --> 00:01:14.320
a better understanding of the overall category performance.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.624
The Filter Results feature helps

00:01:16.624 --> 00:01:21.160
you narrow down your search to identify opportunities that align with your goals.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:22.831
You can create

00:01:22.831 --> 00:01:27.732
highly specific filter combinations paired with sorting to focus on the most relevant

00:01:27.732 --> 00:01:29.240
niches to your strategy.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:32.980
For example, if you want to find popular products within your

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:38.810
target price range, you can set a price range using the average price filter, then sort

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.760
by search volume in descending order.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.679
If you sort again by number of top-clicked products,

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:49.280
you can spot potential niches where demand is growing, but competition isn't high.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:49.613
Once

00:01:49.613 --> 00:01:55.280
you've identified a niche you'd like to explore further, click the niche to see in-depth metrics.

00:01:55.820 --> 00:02:01.430
Navigate to the Insights and Trends tab and toggle between Views to analyze your competition

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:03.300
and track your customer performance.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:08.007
Select up to two metrics to plot in the chart and

00:02:08.007 --> 00:02:10.820
view seasonal shopping patterns and spot growth opportunities.

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.696
For example, comparing search

00:02:12.696 --> 00:02:19.262
volume with search conversion rate can reveal when customers are searching versus when they're

00:02:19.262 --> 00:02:24.380
actually buying, which can be insightful for timing promotions or product launches.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:26.082
Use the

00:02:26.082 --> 00:02:30.600
average selling price metric to understand how price changes affect sales.

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:31.785
If you notice

00:02:31.785 --> 00:02:36.525
that search conversion only increases when prices decline, consider building this into

00:02:36.525 --> 00:02:41.660
your margin and pricing model before launching a new product in this space.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:42.809
Use pricing history

00:02:42.809 --> 00:02:48.940
to understand the best time to run deals and drop prices to ensure you're staying competitive.

00:02:48.940 --> 00:02:54.593
A high average price, along with high search conversion rates, may suggest a less competitive

00:02:54.593 --> 00:03:01.000
niche or a space where customers are willing to pay a premium price for a popular product.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:06.288
If you create your own products, this could be an opportunity to develop a high quality

00:03:06.288 --> 00:03:07.940
offering at a lower price.

00:03:07.940 --> 00:03:12.450
If you source products, this could be an opportunity to add an offer

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:18.000
to top listings within the niche, especially if you notice a high out of stock rate.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:18.449
Comparing

00:03:18.449 --> 00:03:24.730
metrics like selling partner count, brand count, or product count alongside search volume can

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:28.320
help you assess how competitive a niche is.

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:31.758
High demand with a low selling partner or product

00:03:31.758 --> 00:03:37.632
count can represent an opportunity to enter a less competitive niche, whereas a consistently low

00:03:37.632 --> 00:03:44.320
brand count can suggest that a niche is dominated by particular brands already in the space.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:44.691
High

00:03:44.691 --> 00:03:49.520
product count with steady growth could suggest a niche is becoming more competitive.

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.344
Navigate to

00:03:50.344 --> 00:03:56.520
the search terms tab and sort by total count and search conversion in descending order.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:57.411
Look for

00:03:57.411 --> 00:04:02.760
terms with crossover between high search volume and high search conversion rates.

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:03.738
This overlap

00:04:03.738 --> 00:04:07.160
helps reveal customer demand and valued features.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:09.560
Be sure to pay attention to click share.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.354
A high

00:04:10.354 --> 00:04:14.720
click share with low conversion may suggest an unmet customer demand.

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:16.560
Customer feedback is also

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.160
a great strategy to use for informing your product selections.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:22.994
Watch the customer reviews

00:04:22.994 --> 00:04:27.120
insights overview video in Seller Central to learn more.
